the phone number requirement for Call of  Duty has been clarified and Gotham  Knights is getting an exciting new mode  Activision has clarified the SMS  requirement for Call Of Duty Modern  Warfare 2 confirming that a phone number  is required for PC players but not on  Console this confirmation comes not long  after another Activision Blizzard game  OverWatch 2 made headlines for its own  controversial SMS policy in a blog post  Activision said a quote text enabled  mobile phone number is required for  Modern Warfare 2 on PC this is the same  requirement that has been in place for  war zone players on PC since May of 2020  anyone who previously played Warzone on  PC won't have to do anything else to get  started with Modern Warfare 2 and  Warzone 2.0 additionally people on Steam  must link a phone number to play Modern  Warfare 2 so this requirement is not  limited to Battle.net alone the SMS  verification requirement is in place to  help with the anti-cheat efforts and  Activision added the requirement for  Call Of Duty Modern Warfare 2019 PC  players in August of 2022. Activision  also provided an update on the efforts  it's taking to fight cheating in Modern  Warfare 2 and Warzone 2.0 Activision's  Ricochet anti-cheat system will be  available at launch for MW2 and Warzone  2.0 and it will be beefed up with quote  better detection capabilities additional  access to develop and deploy new  mitigation techniques and expanded  freedom to update the security more  frequently than ever before during the  Modern Warfare 2 Beta the Ricochet  anti-cheat tools held the Activision ban  20 000 cheaters from the early test  additionally Activision banned sixty  thousand illicit accounts before the  beta even began Call of Duty Modern  Warfare 2 Launches on October 28th but  people who pre-order the game can start  playing The Campaign on October 20th  Activision is encouraging people to play  to its completion by offering special  bonuses and perks for those who complete  the entire thing and now let's talk a  little bit about Gotham Knights the  upcoming brawler set in the Batman  Universe will get a proper four-player  co-op mode in late November a little  over a month after the game's October  21st release called heroic assault the  mode will be added to Gotham Knights as  a free update on November 29th and is  entirely separate from the main story  campaign according to an FAQ on the  Gotham Knight's website the mode will  support up to four players online and  provides a dedicated arena-like  environment for specific objectives to  complete and enemies to defeat on each  floor there will be 30 floors total at  launch for players to complete this mode  will give players yet another way to  experience Co-op as the game's main  story only supports up to two players  heroic assault will allow for each of  the game's four playable characters to  fight crime together as a team in a way  that's not possible in that story mode  but it's Friday so let me know what  you're going to be playing this weekend  I just tried out Spirit fair for the  first time on Steam deck and wow I heard  it was a good game but like that game  that game is pretty adorable so I'm  going to be diving into that more this  weekend among other random things so let  me know in the comments and I'll see you  on Monday
 

